e2e/test-results
e2e/playwright-report

# Worktrees Claude Code agents create for parallel work.
.claude/worktrees/

# A reference file the owner shares into the repo root; never part of the product.
FleetBook_*.html
bash.exe.stackdump
# Spreadsheets dropped in the repo root while testing an import or an export.
# Three of them (uber.xlsx, a generated SIMULIERT_ workbook and a scratch file)
# were swept into a commit by `git add -A` on 22.10.2026 and reached staging:
# 898 KB of a real customer's ride export and a simulated Fahrtenbuch, neither
# of which belongs in version control. Put a sample under tests/fixtures/ with
# a name that says what it is, or keep it outside the checkout.
# The two rules below were ROOT-ONLY (the leading slash), so a workbook one
# directory down was never ignored: on 26.10.2026 `corection/` held a real
# Fahrtenbuch export and one `git add -A` would have published it, which is
# the same accident as 22.10 with the subdirectory left open. This repository
# is public. So: any spreadsheet, anywhere, unless it is a named fixture.
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
*.xls
*.csv
SIMULIERT_*.xlsx
# A fixture is opted IN by path, so a sample with a name that says what it is
# stays in version control and nothing else does.
!tests/fixtures/**/*.xlsx
!tests/fixtures/**/*.csv
!src/**/__fixtures__/**/*.csv
# The owner's own working folders: audit reports, prompts and real exports.
# `w/` joined the list on 27.10.2026, carrying audit round 2's evidence.
#
# Note WHY a folder rule is needed beside the extension rules above, because
# the extension rules would not have saved us: that evidence arrived as a
# PASTED MARKDOWN TABLE — `w/Pasted markdown(20261027-075704).md`, 222 rows
# holding four drivers' names and 222 real street addresses. No `*.xlsx` or
# `*.csv` rule matches a `.md` file, and `*.md` cannot be ignored in a
# repository whose documentation is Markdown. A ride export is customer data
# whatever extension it is pasted into, so the folder is the unit that is
# ignored, not the file type.
corection/
w/
# The external auditor's own packages, as they arrive. Round 3's holds the
# reply under review plus the round's reports; the earlier rounds' evidence
# carried four drivers' names and 222 real street addresses, and nothing in
# such a package has been checked for customer data before it lands in the
# checkout. Ignored as a folder, for the reason above: a ride export is
# customer data whatever extension it is pasted into.
FleetBook_Round*/
FleetBook_*_Package/
